Lab 11: Manage Access for Automation Controller
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Create and manage users and teams in Ansible Automation Controller
Configure role-based access control (RBAC) for different user types
Assign appropriate permissions to users and teams based on organizational roles
Test access control by logging in with different user accounts
Understand the security implications of proper access management
Implement best practices for user and team management in enterprise automation environments
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with Ansible concepts and terminology
Knowledge of user management principles
Understanding of role-based access control concepts
Completed previous Ansible Automation Controller labs or equivalent experience
Basic understanding of web-based administration interfaces
